The group runs through the Dangai as the walls behind them collapse and the Kōryū begins catching up. Uryū looks back at the encroaching current, prompting Yoruichi to scold him for wasting time. She warns them that if the Kōryū engulfs them, they are finished.

A mass of the Kōryū surges toward the group. They dodge it, but it catches Uryū's cape and starts dragging him backward. Ichigo curses the ridiculous outfit that caused the problem and reaches for Zangetsu, intending to cut Uryū free.

Yoruichi immediately warns Ichigo not to use his Zanpakutō. Spiritual beings who expose or use their Zanpakutō in the Kōryū become entangled in the current themselves. Ichigo asks what he is supposed to do, but Chad acts before he can get an answer. He tears Uryū's cape free and carries him away while continuing to run. Uryū protests that Chad should put him down.

While looking back, Uryū notices something approaching behind them and asks what it is. Yoruichi identifies it as the Kōtotsu, the Cleaner of the Dangai. It appears once every seven days, and they must flee before it catches them. Yoruichi urges them to hurry because the exit is close.

The Kōtotsu rapidly closes the distance. Uryū realizes that they cannot outrun it. Orihime stops, turns around, and summons her Shun Shun Rikka. She activates Santen Kesshun, placing her shield between the group and the approaching Cleaner.

The collision produces a tremendous burst of force that sends everyone out of the Dangai and into Soul Society. Orihime uses her abilities to catch the falling group and cushion their landing in the Rukongai. Once everyone has recovered, the group continues toward the Seireitei.
